#hasheq((campaign . "v1.00.24-test-design-hotspot-remediation") (kind . "wave-review") (notes . ("seam ownership: current-gsd-timeout-now-ms / current-gsd-timeout-wait are the only clock/wait entry points consulted by run-wave-with-timeout; production defaults are exactly current-inexact-milliseconds and sync/timeout with the unchanged 0.1s poll quantum and two-second cancel grace" "determinism: tests/helpers/gsd-timeout-fake.rkt advances only on advance-seconds! and delivers completion/cancellation via semaphores, so no test reimplements timeout logic and no wall-clock sleep remains in the fast timeout tests" "cancel exactly once: stop-runner! contains the single (gsd-wave-runner-port-cancel!) call site; the fake's cancel count asserts exactly-once for cancel-wins, deadline, and completion paths" "outcome exactly once: wait! result is returned directly (not re-synced), so 'timed-out / 'cancelled / runner outcome is emitted exactly once; DONE-still-false-on-timeout and retry-count isolation assertions preserved" "thread/custodian hygiene: worker thread is killed only after the grace wait, kill only when (thread-dead?) is false, no custodian added, no leaked ports in tests (fake ports are plain structs, semaphores are the only sync objects)" "dynamic-parameter inheritance: worker thread is created inside run-wave-with-timeout, so the caller's parameterization is inherited; parameter guards reject non-thunk/non-2-arity fakes at install time" "real-clock coverage retained: test-gsd-wave-timeout-canary.rkt re-tiers to @speed slow (L4) and proves cooperative cancel (no 2s grace), force-kill reaping (cancel-ignoring runner), and DONE-not-written-on-timeout with a <=12s total cap tolerating CI jitter" "ledger/ownership: deterministic timeout semantics remain fast, real clock/thread integration owned by the L4 canary; v124-behavior-table rows added and regenerated ownership/ledger outputs match byte-for-byte (ownership check: 12 behaviors, 0 errors)" "scope disclosure: a follow-up hardening commit (1034106f) made the /go executor deadline mandatory — run-campaign-wave now wraps every runner with run-wave-with-timeout using current-gsd-wave-timeout-seconds (configured default 7200, unchanged) when #:timeout-sec is absent, removing the raw unbounded-port fallback; timeout values, retry ceiling, cancellation policy, status mapping, and user messages are unchanged, and deterministic seam regression tests cover both files")) (reviewer . "q-agent-independent-review") (scope . "GSD wave deadline/event seam; timeout suite determinism; L4 timeout canary") (status . "completed") (verdict . "pass") (wave . "W4"))
